<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,430.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,430.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,430 today from 1,419 on March 6, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dlrs per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate </p>
<p>   1    1479    13.431	  1481    13.444</p>
<p>   1a   1442 10925.000	  1433 10856.000</p>
<p>   2    1730    24.719	  1717    24.531</p>
<p>   2a   1770 14519.000	  1741 14281.000</p>
<p>   3    1624    14.981	  1619    14.938</p>
<p>   3a   1454 11475.000	  1444 11400.000</p>
